; Edit > Logical Editor picks notes by a condition — their pitch, length, the
; voice or sample they play — in the selection, the channel at the cursor or
; the whole score, and acts on all of them at once: transpose, set or scale
; their length, reverse the run, turn them into rests, or just select them.
; Apply writes the score, one undo step.
; Try: transpose fm2 up an octave with the Logical Editor: the cursor in fm2, Scope "Channel at the cursor", Do "Transpose" 12.
(fm1 c e g e c e g e)
(fm2 :oct 2 c2 g2)
